The Ash Plea was Rakuen's second annexation attempt, filed as an emergency humanitarian appeal during late Ash-and-Iron instability.
Rakuen requested integration support tied to route collapse, ration stress, and population displacement pressure.
Midgaard refused on route-instability and administrative-practicality grounds.
The non-binding route-stability talks that followed produced no durable obligations.
